Z||000000||FLASHY||09-21-2001||08:49 PM||||The cables that hold my lid from slamming into the back window broke a long time ago. Now thanks to Voytek I'm the proud owner of a gas shock that holds the lid in place. He picked one up for me at the wrecker which came off a Cadillac. It works REALLY well!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunkshock1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunkshock2.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flash_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||14
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||09-21-2001||09:07 PM||||Hey!  Looks good!  It's too bad I didn't get to spend much time at the meeting last night, so I didn't notice (unless you put those on today).<P>On a side note, I bought a blacklight from Wal-Mart, and the gauges I was telling you about.  They'll be installed by the Red Deer run, so (if you're going) you'll get to see 'em then!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FLASHY||09-21-2001||09:36 PM||||Cool! I'll be there so I'll see it then.<P>I just installed the shock today so that's why you didn't see it. Take it easy man.||||reg||1
