Z||000004||qwikgta||09-22-2001||01:32 AM||||Cool...I got mine off a 84 Buick Regal front hood, I mounted mine the other way.  Here is a shot for you to see what it would look like.<P>Rob<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strutshot_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FLASHY||09-22-2001||04:48 AM||||It takes about ten minutes if you have the right bolt size. You just need longer ones to allow the thickness of the shock to fit in between. I shimmed mine up with washers as well to keep the alignment fairly straight. Very quick and easy.||||reg||1
